            "criterionId": "AC-positive",
            "severity": "blocking",
            "observed": "The new add implementation in sum.mjs declares a local variable named TOTAL in UPPER_CASE: 'export const add = (left, right) => { const TOTAL = left + right; return TOTAL; };'. This breaks the declared lowerCamelCase rule for locals in sum.mjs. A lowerCamelCase name such as total, or simply returning left + right directly, would follow the convention.",
            "expected": "Local variables in sum.mjs use lowerCamelCase.",
            "reproductionSteps": [
              "Read CONVENTIONS.md and find: 'Local variables in sum.mjs use lowerCamelCase.'",
              "Read the sum.mjs hunk in the candidate diff and see that it adds 'const TOTAL = left + right; return TOTAL;'.",
